Z||000158||Greg Piet||01-31-2001||04:08 PM||||OK with now the X-Files disappearing mistertwo owners, I will just bring up the silly idea that all IP's are logged here on PFF.<BR>It is possible to get the IP of a person as a admin and then do a crosscheck on the IP's used by all others.<P>Typically even under dynamic IP assignment with cablemodems, DSL their IP's stay the same since typically once a network card gets an IP it gets the same IP untill the "lease" runs out.  My cable modem service typically has 60 days before the possibility of me getting a different IP.  I have never gotten a different IP with the same net card in over a year.  It gets trickier with dial ups(like AOHELL), but the IP could at least be traced to canada, and possibly toronto...<P>For example the first 2 sets of numbers of the IP I am on now is used by my university.<P>And doing a traceroute will give you my computers domain name which will tell you I am at an educational institution.||||reg||1
